{"kind": "simulate", "reply": "This is only a what-if, and nothing was saved. If the ₱50,000 bonus goes on the credit card now, and you keep putting ₱10,000.00 a month on it, the balance drops from ₱76,880.00 to ₱26,880.00. The card would then be paid off in 3 months, on Mar 1, 2027, instead of 7 months (Jul 1, 2027). Interest on the card falls from ₱9,358.80 to ₱1,351.70.

The money freed up after that then goes to the car loan, so it would be paid off on Jul 1, 2028 instead of Oct 1, 2028. Its interest falls from ₱38,914.35 to ₱32,934.50.

